          "guid": "msz911q5yzadqyxg",
          "message": {
            "text": "Presentation is derived from Unicode properties and the exact variation-selector sequence, while color ownership is measured from the live resolved font cascade. This replaces the missing Geometric Shapes special case with the same general decision Blink makes: U+25FD/U+25FE default to emoji presentation, VS15 requests text, VS16 requests emoji, and the selected face's actual paint determines raster versus vector.",
            "markdown": "Presentation is derived from Unicode properties and the exact variation-selector sequence, while color ownership is measured from the live resolved font cascade. This replaces the missing Geometric Shapes special case with the same general decision Blink makes: U+25FD/U+25FE default to emoji presentation, VS15 requests text, VS16 requests emoji, and the selected face's actual paint determines raster versus vector."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/script/emoji-detect.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 301,
                  "endLine": 314,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    // Variation selectors and default presentation are Unicode properties,\n    // while whether the selected face is actually a color font is a live\n    // cascade result. Probe that exact sequence instead of maintaining another\n    // block/codepoint table parallel to Blink + ICU.\n    if (nextCp === 0xFE0E && RE_EMOJI_PROP.test(String.fromCodePoint(cp))) {\n      const live = textPresentationPaintsColor(cp, font);\n      return live ?? false;\n    }\n    if (nextCp === 0xFE0F && RE_EMOJI_PROP.test(String.fromCodePoint(cp))) {\n      return isColorGlyph(cp, font, '\\uFE0F') || ignoresFillColor(cp, font, '\\uFE0F');\n    }\n    // `rasterCps` (the ✨ ❌ ➡ checkmark/star family) are codepoints Chrome\n    // routes to the COLOR emoji font even when a text font in the cascade has\n    // a monochrome glyph — emoji presentation wins regardless of the author's"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
